Description: End the speech audio export only when its renderer stops advancing
 The renderer reports its phases and, once its consumer runs, each frame it
 handled. The editor counts those as progress, and before the consumer runs
 also the processor time the renderer uses, since a long project loads inside
 one phase with nothing to report. After 20 seconds without progress the export
 is ended and said, and the editor's log keeps the renderer's state at that
 moment: alive or gone, its phase, its last frame, its threads and the
 processor time it used. A slow start or a slow export is never ended.
Origin: vendor
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-26

